"""The fresh everyday-intent queries for books-extra.jsonl and how each one's acceptable books are chosen.

Written from the catalogue's metadata alone, before any embedding was scored: a query's right books are every book whose
TITLE (and, for Gutenberg, author / LCC shelf) clearly covers the topic, exactly the standard of `books.jsonl`
("nobody read the books"). `sl` is a regex over the Survivor Library title, `gut` one over the Gutenberg title (with an
optional shelf-prefix regex and an optional exclusion). The Survivor category is NOT used to pick answers: the site's
category is one of the representations under test, so gold picked by it would be circular.
"""
